<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The English copy, for a handset set to English.

  Indonesian is the default in `values/` because these customers and their accounts are Indonesian,
  and a handset set to anything else falls back to it. This file is the one exception the platform
  picks up on its own — no code chooses it, and nothing here is about the *conversation* language,
  which the customer switches inside a conversation and which follows the words they use.

  The personas' own names are deliberately absent: Rendra is Rendra in both languages, so the picker
  carries them in code rather than keeping a second copy here that could drift.
-->
